IMPORT prelude

-- Public Service (Monthly Variable Component and Non-pensionable Annual Allowance) Act 1988 (Singapore) -- who is in the "public
-- service" (s 2), the Minister's power to vary the monthly variable component and the 13th month non-pensionable annual allowance,
-- the duty to give effect to an order and the voiding of contractual terms in excess of it (s 3), and pensions computed as if the
-- monthly variable component had not been reduced (s 4).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PSMVCNAAA1988.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". Its Legislative
-- History lists no amending Act after Act 14 of 1988 -- only the 1989 and 2014 Revised Editions (and a predecessor, Act 19 of 1987,
-- the Public Service (Variation of 1984 Annual Wage Increases) Act 1987).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0199 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The whole operative Act (ss 2-4) is encoded; it is four sections long.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the contents of any order under s 3(1) (none was retrieved, so every rate and amount here is a stated fact, not a
-- figure from an order); which statutory bodies the Minister has designated by Gazette notification; how the Pensions Act 1956 and the
-- Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978 then compute a pension from the figure s 4 hands them.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example naive rows. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Service (Monthly Variable Component and Non-pensionable Annual Allowance) Act 1988 -- nouns`

DECLARE Employer IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `a designated statutory body`
    `an undesignated statutory body`
    `a private employer`

DECLARE `Source of the term` IS ONE OF
    `a contract of employment`
    `a collective agreement`
    `a scheme of service`

DECLARE `Pension law` IS ONE OF
    `the Pensions Act 1956`
    `the Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978`
    `some other law or scheme`

§§ `2 -- public service`

-- s 2: "monthly variable component" means "the aggregate of the annual wage increases for the years 1982 to 1984 payable pursuant to
-- the recommendations of the National Wages Council".
-- "public service" means "service under the Government and includes -- (a) service as the holder of any public office or service as a
-- Member of Parliament; and (b) service under any statutory body or authority designated by the Minister by notification in the
-- Gazette."
GIVEN `serves under the Government` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds a public office` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a Member of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `serves under a statutory body` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the body is designated by Gazette notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is public service` IF
        `serves under the Government`
    OR  `holds a public office`
    OR  `is a Member of Parliament`
    OR  (`serves under a statutory body` AND `the body is designated by Gazette notification`)

§§ `3 -- the Minister's order`

-- s 3(1): "The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, vary in such manner as may be specified in the order -- (a) the rates of the
-- monthly variable component; and (b) the amount of the 13th month non-pensionable annual allowance, payable to the public service."
-- (2): "When any order under subsection (1) comes into force, the Government and any designated statutory body or authority must give
-- effect to the order."
GIVEN `the employer` IS AN Employer, `an order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must give effect to the order` IF
    `an order is in force` AND
    (CONSIDER `the employer`
     WHEN `the Government` THEN TRUE
     WHEN `a designated statutory body` THEN TRUE
     OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- s 3(3): "Any term or condition of employment in the public service (including any collective agreement) imposing any liability to
-- pay -- (a) rates of monthly variable component; or (b) the amount of the 13th month non-pensionable annual allowance, in excess of
-- the rates or amount specified in the order is, to the extent of the excess, void and of no effect so long as the order remains in
-- force."
-- The same rule applies to both heads, so one pair of functions serves the monthly variable component and the 13th month allowance.
-- The source of the term does not matter: "any term or condition", "including any collective agreement".
GIVEN `the source` IS A `Source of the term`, `in the public service` IS A BOOLEAN, `an order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the term promises` IS A NUMBER, `the order specifies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the void excess` IS
    IF `in the public service` AND `an order is in force` AND `the term promises` GREATER THAN `the order specifies`
    THEN `the term promises` MINUS `the order specifies`
    ELSE 0

-- What the term can still be enforced for: the promise less the void excess. "to the extent of the excess" -- the rest of the term
-- stands; "so long as the order remains in force" -- when the order ceases, nothing is void.
GIVEN `the source` IS A `Source of the term`, `in the public service` IS A BOOLEAN, `an order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the term promises` IS A NUMBER, `the order specifies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the term is enforceable for` IS
    `the term promises` MINUS (`the void excess` `the source` `in the public service` `an order is in force` `the term promises` `the order specifies`)

-- INFERENCE, not stated in s 3: where an order specifies MORE than the term promises, s 3(3) voids nothing, but s 3(2) obliges the
-- Government or designated body to "give effect to the order". This function reads that as: the employer pays what the order
-- specifies. For an employer s 3(2) does not bind, the term is left as it is.
GIVEN `the employer` IS AN Employer, `in the public service` IS A BOOLEAN, `an order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the term promises` IS A NUMBER, `the order specifies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount the employer pays` IS
    IF `in the public service` AND `the employer must give effect to the order` `the employer` `an order is in force`
    THEN `the order specifies`
    ELSE `the term promises`

§§ `4 -- pensions not to be affected`

-- s 4: "All pensions, gratuities and other allowances to be granted under the Pensions Act 1956 and the Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978
-- to any person must be computed as if the monthly variable component applicable to that person had not been reduced by virtue of any
-- order made or continued in force under this Act."
-- Only a REDUCTION is disregarded: an order that raises the component is not undone. The section names the monthly variable component
-- only, not the 13th month allowance (which is, by its name, non-pensionable).
GIVEN `the law` IS A `Pension law`, `the component before any order` IS A NUMBER, `the component under the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the component the pension is computed on` IS
    IF `s 4 protects` `the law` AND `the component under the order` LESS THAN `the component before any order`
    THEN `the component before any order`
    ELSE `the component under the order`

GIVEN `the law` IS A `Pension law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4 protects` IF
    CONSIDER `the law`
    WHEN `the Pensions Act 1956` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
